WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.960
1 of 6. Understand the change request
Open Change request to read the requested behavior and constraints. Identify what should change and what existing behavior must keep working.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.800
2 of 6. Make a focused change
From Change request, open Edit files. The workspace’s Edit changes view holds the editable files for this request. Keep the change small enough to explain and check the save status before testing.

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.520
3 of 6. Check for regressions
Open Edit files to run tests when the runner is available, then inspect Execution evidence. Use failures to revise the change; an unavailable run supplies no regression evidence.

4
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:24.360
4 of 6. Explain the pull request
Use Files changed here, or Pull request in the editing workspace, to review saved changes and their evidence. Explain the intended effect, compatibility risks and checks so the change can be assessed.

5
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:30.720
5 of 6. Use the review to finish the change
Submit your saved work when ready. Read the recorded feedback and revise any gaps before submitting again. A documentation edit or successful test run alone does not complete the phase.

6
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:41.360
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
